.TH _printf 3
.SH NAME
_printf \- custom implementation of the C standard printf function

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The _printf function produces output according to a specified format and
writes the result to the standard output (stdout). It processes the format
string character-by-character. When it encounters a percent sign (%), it
identifies the following character as a format specifier and handles it
accordingly.

Supported format specifiers include:
.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a null-terminated string.
.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal percent sign.
.TP
.B %d, %i
Prints a signed integer.

Text that does not include a percent sign is written directly to the output.
If a NULL format string is passed, or if the format ends with a lone percent
sign (e.g., "%"), the function returns -1 to indicate an error.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The _printf function returns the total number of characters printed.
If an error occurs, the function returns -1.

.SH EXAMPLES
.B Example 1:
_printf("Hello %s\n", "Fahad");

.B Example 2:
_printf("Value: %d\n", 123);

.B Example 3:
_printf("Percent sign: %%\n");

